  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInAndImportantAdditionsToFranchiseRightsTextBlock id="Tag857" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInAndImportantAdditionsToFranchiseRightsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfAcquisitionOfOwnershipInOtherCompaniesByReorganizationMergerOrConsolidationWithOtherCompaniesTextBlock id="Tag858" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfAcquisitionOfOwnershipInOtherCompaniesByReorganizationMergerOrConsolidationWithOtherCompaniesTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfPurchaseOrSaleOfAnOperatingUnitOrSystemTextBlock id="Tag859" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Not applicable&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfPurchaseOrSaleOfAnOperatingUnitOrSystemTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantLeaseholdsThatHaveBeenAcquiredOrGivenAssignedOrSurrenderedTextBlock id="Tag860" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Not applicable&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantLeaseholdsThatHaveBeenAcquiredOrGivenAssignedOrSurrenderedTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantExtensionOrReductionOfTransmissionOrDistributionSystemTextBlock id="Tag861" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantExtensionOrReductionOfTransmissionOrDistributionSystemTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock id="Tag862" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: .25in; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .25in 256.5pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="mso-list: Ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;!--[endif]--&gt;On December 31, 2023, NYISO entered into a $50.0 million Revolving Line of Credit with an effective date of January 1, 2024 through December 31, 2028. This financing was approved by the New York Public Service Commission in CASE 23-E-0293&lt;strong&gt;. &lt;/strong&gt;The proceeds from this Revolving Line of Credit are used to provide liquidity for&amp;#160;NYISO&amp;#8217;s&amp;#160;markets from 2024 to 2028. Interest on borrowings under this Term Loan Facility is based on&amp;#160;NYISO&amp;#8217;s&amp;#160;option of varying rates of interest tied to either the prime rate or the SOFR. As of December 31, 2025, there were no outstanding borrowings from the revolving line of credit facility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoListParagraph"&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: .25in; text-indent: -.25in; tab-stops: list .25in;"&gt;&lt;font style="mso-tab-count: 1;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;On December 31, 2023, NYISO entered a $100.0 million Revolving Term Loan Credit Facility which is used for capital purchases and significant projects during 2024 -2028. This financing was approved by the New York Public Service Commission in CASE 23-E-0293&lt;strong&gt;.&amp;#160;&lt;/strong&gt;In 2024, $37.0 million was borrowed against the unsecured credit facility, which was converted to a term loan in January 2025 payable over three years. As of December 31, 2025, $18.4 million is outstanding on 2024 borrowings. As of September 30, 2025, $37.0M is outstanding on 2025 borrowings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: .25in; text-indent: -.25in; tab-stops: list .25in;"&gt;&lt;font style="background: yellow; mso-highlight: yellow;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: .25in; text-indent: -.25in; tab-stops: list .25in;"&gt;&lt;font style="mso-tab-count: 1;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;On December 14, 2018, NYISO entered into a $90.0 million unsecured line of credit which to fund capital purchases, with an effective date of January 1, 2019 through December 31, 2023. This financing was approved by the New York Public Service Commission in CASE 18-E-0439. In 2019, $26.0 million was borrowed the unsecured credit facility, which was converted to a term loan in January 2020 payable over three years.&amp;#160; The 2019 borrowings have been repaid in full.&amp;#160; In 2020, an additional $26.6 million was borrowed from the unsecured credit facility, which was converted to a term loan in January 2021 payable over three years. The 2020 borrowings have been repaid in full.&amp;#160; In 2021, an additional $28.4 million was borrowed from the unsecured credit facility, which was converted to a term loan in January 2022. The 2021 borrowings have been repaid in full.&amp;#160; In 2022, an additional $32.0 million was borrowed from the unsecured credit facility, which was converted to a term loan in January 2023. The 2022 borrowings have been repaid in full.&amp;#160; In 2023, an additional $27.0 million was borrowed from the unsecured credit facility, which was converted to a term loan in January 2024.&amp;#160; As of December 31, 2025, $6.2 million is outstanding on 2023 borrowings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInArticlesOfIncorporationOrAmendmentsToCharterTextBlock id="Tag863" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInArticlesOfIncorporationOrAmendmentsToCharterTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedAnnualEffectAndNatureOfAnyImportantWageScaleChangesTextBlock id="Tag864" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: .25in; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .25in 256.5pt;"&gt;As a whole, merit wage increases were &lt;font style="background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;"&gt;approximately 2.1%&lt;/font&gt; from 2024 to 2025.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedAnnualEffectAndNatureOfAnyImportantWageScaleChangesTextBlock>
