&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 10pt;"&gt;NYISO invoices market participants weekly for settlement charges and Rate Schedule&amp;#160;1 revenue. As of December&amp;#160;31, 2025, current&amp;#8209;due settlement invoices represented amounts invoiced on December&amp;#160;31, 2025 for the period December&amp;#160;13 through December&amp;#160;19, 2025, and were collected on January&amp;#160;5, 2026. As of December 31, 2024, current-due settlement invoices represented amounts invoiced on December 31, 2024 for the period December 21 through December 27, and were collected on January 3, 2025.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 10pt;"&gt;Miscellaneous billed and unbilled receivables are for planning study services provided by the NYISO in accordance with the NYISO OATT. These revenues offset the corresponding planning study expenses, which are incurred in performing such studies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 10pt;"&gt;NYISO recovers its Rate Schedule&amp;#160;1 revenue in the invoice following the period of service. Therefore, a portion of unbilled Rate Schedule&amp;#160;1 revenues for December&amp;#160;are billed and recovered in January&amp;#160;of the subsequent year. The unbilled revenues were for the period December&amp;#160;20, 2025 to December&amp;#160;31, 2025. The unbilled revenues as of December 31, 2024 were for the period December 28, 2024 to December 31, 2024.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; text-indent: -17.97pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '(%0)'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '3'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 5.75pt; -aw-outline-level: 1;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;(3)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 5.75pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Regulatory Assets and Liabilities&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 10pt; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;At December&amp;#160;31, 2025 and 2024, regulatory assets and liabilities consisted of the following:&lt;/p&gt;
